gyb(){return"Your Road to 100 Push Ups"},
gxS(){return"We'll build a personalized daily plan that takes you from where you are today to 100 consecutive push ups \u2014 no gym, no equipment, just a few minutes a day."},
gxY(){return"Chest, shoulders, triceps, and core \u2014 a classic compound push movement that builds upper-body pressing strength and full-body stability."},
gxM(){return"No equipment, no gym membership, works anywhere \u2014 one of the most efficient ways to build real upper-body strength using just your bodyweight."},
gy5(){return"100 consecutive push ups is a widely recognized benchmark of upper-body endurance \u2014 most people who train consistently for a few months can reach it, regardless of where they start."},
gye(){return"Your Road to 100 Squats"},
gxV(){return"We'll build a personalized daily plan that takes you from your current max to 100 consecutive squats \u2014 just your bodyweight and a few minutes a day."},
gy0(){return"Quads, glutes, and hamstrings \u2014 the squat is the foundation movement for lower-body strength and everyday functional mobility."},
gxP(){return"Builds lower-body strength and mobility that carries over to walking, climbing stairs, and everyday movement \u2014 no equipment required."},
gy8(){return"100 consecutive squats is a well-known strength-endurance milestone \u2014 achievable by most people with a gradual, progressive plan, even starting from zero."},
gya(){return"Your Road to 50 Pull Ups"},
gxR(){return"We'll build a personalized daily plan that takes you from your current max to 50 consecutive pull ups \u2014 the plan adapts to your own pace."},
gxX(){return"Back, biceps, and grip \u2014 one of the toughest bodyweight pulling movements, and one of the best builders of true upper-body pulling strength."},
gxL(){return"Pull ups train a muscle group most pushing-focused routines neglect \u2014 a stronger back and grip translate directly into better posture and pulling power in daily life."},
gy4(){return"50 consecutive pull ups is an elite-level benchmark \u2014 few people ever reach it, so your plan sets realistic intermediate milestones along the way instead of expecting a straight line from day one."},
gy9(){return"Your Road to a 5-Minute Plank"},
gxQ(){return"We'll build a personalized daily plan that takes you from your current hold time to a full 5-minute plank \u2014 a few focused minutes a day, growing gradually."},
gxW(){return"Core, shoulders, and glutes \u2014 an isometric hold that builds deep core stability and postural endurance, not just visible abs."},
gxK(){return"Core stability is the foundation almost every other movement relies on \u2014 a stronger plank means a stronger, more protected lower back in everything else you do."},
gy3(){return"Holding a plank for 5 straight minutes is a recognized core-endurance benchmark, reached through steady week-over-week increases rather than any single big jump."},
gyc(){return"Your Road to a 10K Run"},
gxT(){return"We'll build a personalized daily plan that takes you from your current distance to running 10 kilometers straight \u2014 gradual mileage increases, with rest days built in."},
gxZ(){return"Cardiovascular endurance and leg strength \u2014 running trains your whole aerobic system, not just one muscle group."},
gxN(){return"Running is one of the most accessible ways to build cardiovascular health \u2014 no equipment beyond a pair of shoes, and it's directly tied to long-term heart and metabolic health."},
gy6(){return"10 kilometers is the classic distance milestone for a recreational runner \u2014 a realistic, well-established target for someone building up from a shorter starting distance."},
gyd(){return"Your Road to 200 Sit Ups"},
gxU(){return"We'll build a personalized daily plan that takes you from your current max to 200 consecutive sit ups \u2014 just your bodyweight and a few minutes a day."},
gy_(){return"Abdominals and hip flexors \u2014 a classic core-endurance movement that builds trunk strength through a full range of motion."},
gxO(){return"Builds core endurance that supports posture and protects your lower back during almost every other physical activity \u2014 no equipment required."},
gy7(){return"200 consecutive sit ups is a demanding but achievable core-endurance milestone \u2014 the high rep count is exactly why the plan builds toward it gradually instead of all at once."},
gyh(){return"Uses your phone's proximity sensor. Place it face-up on the floor, right where your face or chest lowers to during the push up. Getting close enough and pulling back again counts as one rep."},
gyk(){return"Uses your phone's accelerometer. Keep it in your front pants or shorts pocket while you squat. Going down and back up counts as one rep."},
